# Physics receipt (dynamics grammar plan, G3): the picker refuses only what
# a law refuses. Still and Anneal are kinematic and take an overlay
# converted (v = F/gamma, the rule Hold follows), so their overlays stay on;
# Density takes Hub room, Centre and Tide converted and disables the rest
# (F73, F81).
assert title GRAPHSHELL H3 READY
assert snap ready == true
select #gs-physics-select anneal.davidson-harel
check #gs-overlay-gravity-locus on
settle 1
assert attr #gs-overlay-note hidden
select #gs-physics-select still.default
settle 1
assert attr #gs-overlay-note hidden
dom click [data-command="apply-physics"]
settle 1
assert snap physics-law == still.default
assert snap physics-overlays == gravity-locus
assert dom #gs-product-status Physics set to Still
select #gs-physics-select density.gastner-newman
settle 1
assert attr #gs-overlay-grid-snap disabled
assert dom #gs-overlay-note Density takes only Hub room, Centre and Tide
log physics converted receipt complete
